#only("1")[#voiceover("Let's dive deeper into each of these factors affecting the time value of money.")]
#only("2")[#voiceover("First, inflation. Over time, inflation erodes the purchasing power of money. This means that a dollar today can buy more than what that same dollar will be able to buy in the future.")]
#only("3")[#voiceover("Second, interest. When you put money in a savings account or bond, it can earn interest over time. This interest increases the future value of your money.")]
#only("4")[#voiceover("Third, investment opportunities. Money that you have today can be invested in stocks, real estate, or a business venture, with the potential to generate returns and grow in value over time.")]
#only("5")[#voiceover("Because of inflation, interest, and investment opportunities, a dollar today is considered more valuable than a dollar in the future. This is the core principle of the time value of money.")]
